.TH SHOAL-HISTORY 1 "July 2026" "Shoal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shoal-history \- query and maintain the Shoal journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shoal-history
.RI [ \-\-state-dir " path" ]
.RI [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries effect history and maintains the journal database and content-addressed storage.
Without an explicit state directory it uses layered
.B journal.state_dir
configuration, then the shared XDG state root.
If COMMAND is omitted,
.B query
is used.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B query
Filter entries with
.BR \-\-since ,
.BR \-\-principal ,
.BR \-\-kind ,
.BR \-\-effects ,
.BR \-\-head ,
.BR \-\-status " ok|failed",
and
.BR \-\-limit .
.TP
.BI show " ID"
Show one entry and its recorded operations.
.TP
.BI pin " HASH"
Retain a content-addressed object during collection.
.TP
.BI unpin " HASH"
Release a retained content-addressed object.
.TP
.B gc
Preview collection; use
.B \-\-ttl SECONDS
and
.B \-\-budget BYTES
to select candidates, and
.B \-\-apply
to delete them.
.TP
.B status
Report journal database, WAL, spill, and CAS use and admission limits.
.TP
.BI undo " ID \-\-root PATH"
Apply the entry's recorded inverse operations below the explicit containment root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-state-dir " PATH"
Override configured and default state storage.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit structured JSON for query, show, status, and undo.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print complete command and filter help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version.
.SH OUTPUT
Query and show render human history by default; status renders storage totals.
JSON mode emits stable structured records.
GC always reports a JSON summary including whether it was a dry run.
.SH ERRORS
Malformed filters, missing values, invalid entry IDs, unknown hashes, missing undo roots,
unknown commands, configuration errors, and journal failures are reported on standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
shoal-history query --status failed --limit 20
shoal-history --json show 42
shoal-history gc --ttl 604800 --budget 1073741824
shoal-history gc --ttl 604800 --apply
shoal-history undo 42 --root ./workspace
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 for missing records and operational failures, and 2 for invalid arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shoal (1)
